 "notes": "Governor field (TSE, 11 candidates): Cleitinho (Republicanos), Patrus Ananias (PT), Kalil (PDT), Mateus Simões (PSD), Flávio Roscoe (PL), Gabriel Azevedo (MDB) named; Ben Mendes (Missão), Túlio Lopes (PCB), Indira Xavier (UP), Henrique Áreas (PCO), Rafael Duda (PSTU) summed in Outros. Patrus only entered the polls in July (earlier PT-allied candidate was Rodrigo Pacheco, PSB, who left the race), so all Jan-Jun polls (AtlasIntel 25-30 Mar, Futura 24-28 Mar, Real Time Big Data 19-20 Mar, Quaest 22-26 Apr, etc.) were skipped: their scenarios have Pacheco and no Patrus. July rows (Quaest 22-26 Jul scenario 1, RTBD 25-29 Jul scenario with Roscoe) include Maria da Consolação (PSOL, ~1-3%, not in the final field) inside Outros. Real Time Big Data 23-26 Sep governor poll published only in valid votes (Cleitinho 41, Patrus 22, Kalil 10, Simões 9, Roscoe 9, Gabriel 5) -> excluded from gov_t1/gov_t2 (its senate numbers are in total, consolidated, and are kept). gov_t2: Cleitinho x Patrus chosen (tied with Cleitinho x Kalil as most-polled, 11 vs 11 polls; Patrus is 2nd in all September polls). Datafolha Aug 18-20 had no 2nd-round data. Wide pollster spread: AtlasIntel and RTBD show Patrus ~30%/~19% vs Quaest/Datafolha 11-16%. Quaest 2026-09-22 senate: minor candidates only reported as <=1% each, so Outros omitted. Carlos Viana listed as PSD per 2026 articles.",
